<title>USA: Hybridon completes $50 mln convertible note sale.</title>
<headline>Hybridon completes $50 mln convertible note sale.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, Mass. 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hybridon Inc said Wednesday it has completed its previously announced offering of nine percent convertible subordinated notes due 2004, in the original purchase amount of $50 million.</p>
<p>The notes, said the company, are convertible into shares of common stock at $7.0125 per share.</p>
<p>Hybridon, a biopharmaceutical company, develops genetic medicines based primarily on antisense technology.</p>
